From 02fdffb0473e4acd06fc9488a6f84621af93ef3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 08:34:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] headless: unchecked bytecode fetch in the COB interpreter

GET_LONG_PC() goes through vector::at() (mantis #5981) so an
out-of-bounds pc on a malformed script throws instead of UB - a
user-facing-client concern. Every opcode and operand word of every COB
script fetches through this macro (CCobThread::Tick, 3.7% self in a
mid-game profile), paying a compare+branch and the exception path's
optimization barrier per word. A headless demo re-sim only runs scripts
that already executed during the live game being replayed, so use the
unchecked [] fetch under HEADLESS. Integer fetches only; identical
values for any valid script - output verified byte-identical via the
snapshot-diff gate.
---
 rts/Sim/Units/Scripts/CobThread.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rts/Sim/Units/Scripts/CobThread.cpp b/rts/Sim/Units/Scripts/CobThread.cpp
index 696471b..13f23c5 100644
--- a/rts/Sim/Units/Scripts/CobThread.cpp
+++ b/rts/Sim/Units/Scripts/CobThread.cpp
@@ -227,7 +227,13 @@ void CCobThread::InitStack(unsigned int n, CCobThread* t)
 	}
 }
 
-#if 0
+#ifdef HEADLESS
+// [barreplay] the .at() below (mantis #5981) turns an out-of-bounds program
+// counter on a MALFORMED script into a catchable exception instead of UB - a
+// user-facing-client concern. A headless demo re-sim only runs scripts that
+// already executed during the live game, so skip the per-fetch bounds check
+// in the interpreter's hottest loop (every opcode + operand word goes through
+// this macro). Integer fetches only - identical values for any valid script.
 #define GET_LONG_PC() (cobFile->code[pc++])
 #else
 // mantis #5981
